   "TrashedCells" -> {".md\nLet's add another PID for ofsetting the angle:", 
     "Block[{}, \n\n]", "{ns} = NDSolve`ProcessEquations[{\n  h[t] == l,\n  \
u'[t] == (*SbB[*)Subscript[K(*|*),(*|*)\"p\"](*]SbB*) h[t] + \
(*SbB[*)Subscript[K(*|*),(*|*)\"i\"](*]SbB*) q + \
(*SbB[*)Subscript[K(*|*),(*|*)\"d\"](*]SbB*) h'[t]\n}, {h,u}, t]", ".md\n## \
Automatic discretization\nLet's try `NDSolve` low-level approach. For this we \
need to keep all equations 1st order:"}|>, 
 "Cells" -> {<|"Data" -> ".md\n# PID Controllers are Fun!\nThis is one of the \
most widely used feedback control mechanisms. You will eventually find it \
everywhere: when you press the gas handle on an e-scooter, set the heater in \
your room, or even flush a toilet.\n\nLet's have a look at the last \
example:\n\n\n<img src=\"/attachments/float-7d9.png\" width=\"512\"/>\n\n", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "8aa4de14-0f71-4c76-a248-a8a9ad0ca40f", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "# PID Controllers are Fun!\nThis is one of the most widely \
used feedback control mechanisms. You will eventually find it everywhere: \
when you press the gas handle on an e-scooter, set the heater in your room, \
or even flush a toilet.\n\nLet's have a look at the last example:\n\n\n<img \
src=\"/attachments/float-7d9.png\" width=\"512\"/>", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "4d0227fc-541b-48d4-8019-a5f8b812802b", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nIn this example, the water level must be full, i.e., if \
we have *a non-zero error* $e(t) = h_{\\text{full}} - h_{\\text{water}}(t)$, \
this will open a valve, i.e., send *a control signal* $u(t)$, which is \
proportional to our error:\n\n$$\nu(t) = K_{p}~e(t)\n$$\n\nOf course, in this \
case $u(t)$ cannot be negative and is clamped to the maximum water flow we \
can have in the system.\n\n## Heater Story\nLet's have a look at the example \
with a heater. \n\n<img \
src=\"/attachments/ChatGPT-Image-Mar-23%2C-2026%2C-05_08_05-PM-cef.png\" \
width=\"500\"/>\n\n\nIt usually takes some time for heat to reach the \
thermometer due to the finite air conductivity as well as the heating \
material. These processes are described by the heat equation\[LongDash]a \
parabolic partial differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial \
t} = \\Delta w\n$$\n\nWe can try to solve it for a 2-dimensional material, \
which is heated from one spot at (-2, 0):\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial \
w}{\\partial t} = \\Delta w + f(x,y,t)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a heating \
function:", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "214f4b49-83b8-47e0-920b-6d363aa353b5", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "In this example, the water level must be full, i.e., if we \
have *a non-zero error* $e(t) = h_{\\text{full}} - h_{\\text{water}}(t)$, \
this will open a valve, i.e., send *a control signal* $u(t)$, which is \
proportional to our error:\n\n$$\nu(t) = K_{p}~e(t)\n$$\n\nOf course, in this \
case $u(t)$ cannot be negative and is clamped to the maximum water flow we \
can have in the system.\n\n## Heater Story\nLet's have a look at the example \
with a heater. \n\n<img \
src=\"/attachments/ChatGPT-Image-Mar-23%2C-2026%2C-05_08_05-PM-cef.png\" \
width=\"500\"/>\n\n\nIt usually takes some time for heat to reach the \
thermometer due to the finite air conductivity as well as the heating \
material. These processes are described by the heat equation\[LongDash]a \
parabolic partial differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial \
t} = \\Delta w\n$$\n\nWe can try to solve it for a 2-dimensional material, \
which is heated from one spot at (-2, 0):\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial \
w}{\\partial t} = \\Delta w + f(x,y,t)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a heating \
function:", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "16f50c4f-55c1-4f0c-a228-246f33c6951e", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "sol = NDSolveValue[\n  {\n    D[w[x, y, t], t] == \
Laplacian[w[x, y, t], {x, y}] + \
If[(*SpB[*)Power[(x+2)(*|*),(*|*)2](*]SpB*)+(*SpB[*)Power[y(*|*),(*|*)2](*]Sp\
B*) < 0.1 && t > 0.0, 100.0, 0],\n    w[x, y, 0] == 0\n  },\n  w,\n  {x, y} \
\[Element] Rectangle[{-2, -1}, {2, 1}],\n  {t, 0, 10}\n];", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "794a79ea-5a3e-4f95-a91d-5b5a8a13707c", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Table[DensityPlot[\n  sol[x,y,t], {x,-2,2}, {y,-1,1}, \n  \
Epilog->{\n    Text[\"\|01f525\", {-2,0}],\n    Text[Style[\"A\", White, \
FontSize->14], {1.6,0.}, {0,0}]\n  },\n  PlotLabel->(\"t = \"<>ToString[t]), \
ColorFunctionScaling->False,\n  ImageSize->200\n], {t, {0.2, 1, 10}}]//Row", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "10c0389b-a787-400b-9fea-a0a76312c1b2", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "(*GB[*){{(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef[\"28dcf07c-ca9a-4ef5-b565-37adbd\
6c571f\"])(*,*)(*\"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkN\
VgEKG1mkJKcZmCfrJidaJuqapKaZ6iaZmpnqGpsnpiSlmCWbmhumAQCUbRZp\"*)(*]VB*)(*|*),\
(*|*)(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef[\"dea8a804-8078-4bca-8d3c-d0f31d616379\"])(*,*)(*\"1\
:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgEKp6QmWiRaGJjoWhiY\
W+iaJCUn6lqkGCfrphikGRummBmaGZtbAgCLZBWn\"*)(*]VB*)(*|*),(*|*)(*VB[*)(FrontEn\
dRef[\"f4c3fcb4-eebd-4aa7-ae1f-1ea4a08f50ad\"])(*,*)(*\"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgE\
SHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgEKp5kkG6clJ5nopqYmpeiaJCaa6yamGqbpGqYm\
miQaWKSZGiSmAACjjBcQ\"*)(*]VB*)}}(*]GB*)", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "367e9801-c028-43a7-a3fe-689b638e4685", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> 
     ".md\nLet's have a look at the fixed `A` point as a function of time:", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "a679be15-ea82-4d1b-bd08-12f979f5c7e9", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> 
     "Let's have a look at the fixed `A` point as a function of time:", 
    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "2b7f9885-f2fe-4518-b8a1-1bd6157ede33", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Plot[sol[1.6,0.,t], {t,0,10}, AxesLabel->{\"time\", \
\"Temperature\"}, PlotLabel->\"A\", PlotRange->Full]", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "cf75e7fd-893b-47b7-b357-18f6a764d395", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef[\"80780f8c-ec23-4ef6-839a-2f426404c55f\"]\
)(*,*)(*\"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgEKWxiYW\
xikWSTrpiYbGeuapKaZ6VoYWybqGqWZGJmZGJgkm5qmAQB/KRVR\"*)(*]VB*)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "2f5e8681-64a2-4a5e-a44b-1e6cf34e33ae", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nThis curve is our system's reaction. It is delayed. \
Unlike electromagnetic or elastic waves, the heat equation describes \
*diffusion waves*. The speed of a diffusion wave is a function of time and \
constantly drops. On the other hand, you can also think about diffusion waves \
as a case of over-damped elastic waves.\n\nWe can't really solve this \
equation including our regulator/controller, since it will invoke a feedback \
loop. This can hardly be solved with `NDSolve` or any other built-in solvers. \
We need to discretize it!", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "8b81956f-a441-4c99-b063-15ec2d1224db", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "This curve is our system's reaction. It is delayed. Unlike \
electromagnetic or elastic waves, the heat equation describes *diffusion \
waves*. The speed of a diffusion wave is a function of time and constantly \
drops. On the other hand, you can also think about diffusion waves as a case \
of over-damped elastic waves.\n\nWe can't really solve this equation \
including our regulator/controller, since it will invoke a feedback loop. \
This can hardly be solved with `NDSolve` or any other built-in solvers. We \
need to discretize it!", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "a1a8a29f-70ac-478d-a92c-a08b0f7aa98b", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## FDTD Method\nTo solve such equations, we can try to \
discretize them in both time and space. It is usually easier to work with 1st \
order differential equations, therefore we introduce 2 helper symbols `vx`, \
`vy`, which are spatial derivatives of `w`:", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "c9ddd347-2288-4442-af40-d864a0a671ed", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "## FDTD Method\nTo solve such equations, we can try to \
discretize them in both time and space. It is usually easier to work with 1st \
order differential equations, therefore we introduce 2 helper symbols `vx`, \
`vy`, which are spatial derivatives of `w`:", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "fadff3da-00f3-4f4c-88c9-94f5a5a4949c", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nLet's write a basic solver for it:", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "bd9d9497-034e-4735-b11f-dca3a50fb0ac", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Let's write a basic solver for it:", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "75af8421-cdba-4177-b7af-48fc29398387", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "solveHeat[w_, f_, dt_:0.0025, dx_:0.1] := Table[\n      \n  \
