    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n### Wheels for the Robot\nWhat about our vehicle? The \
PID controller will certainly control the voltage of the motors or \
current...\n\n> In electric motors (especially DC), voltage determines speed \
(velocity/RPM) and current determines torque (loading force).\n\nThen we go \
with voltage. The revolutions of a wheel will be directly transferred to the \
$x$ coordinate:", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "b0d64c85-4c02-441b-b36b-26968fff5792", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "### Wheels for the Robot\nWhat about our vehicle? The PID \
controller will certainly control the voltage of the motors or \
current...\n\n> In electric motors (especially DC), voltage determines speed \
(velocity/RPM) and current determines torque (loading force).\n\nThen we go \
with voltage. The revolutions of a wheel will be directly transferred to the \
$x$ coordinate:", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "8cb5a454-0456-431a-9c2e-a139540ae3a5", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "createPlatform[initialPos_, mass_] := Module[{stateV = {0., \
0.}, stateX = {1.,1.} initialPos},\n  Function[{u, dt},\n    stateV[[2]] = \
stateV[[1]];\n    (* stateV[[1]] = If[Sign[stateV[[2]]] Sign[u] > 0, Sign[u] \
Max[Abs[u], Abs[stateV[[2]]]], u]; *)\n    stateV[[1]] = \
If[Abs[Abs[stateX[[1]]] - 2.0] < 0.01, 0, u];\n    stateX[[2]] = \
stateX[[1]];\n    stateX[[1]] = Clip[stateX[[2]] + dt stateV[[1]], \
{-2,2}];\n\n    {stateX[[1]], (*FB[*)((stateV[[1]] - \
stateV[[2]])(*,*)/(*,*)(dt))(*]FB*)}\n  ]\n];", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "71a63f3e-6b2d-43f5-a58e-7c8080202f4a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"InitGroup" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nWe made it in a way that if the platform goes too far, \
the motors will stop spinning (vehicle got trapped):", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "c2fa01a5-86b5-4712-9db2-9428fb16130f", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "We made it in a way that if the platform goes too far, the \
motors will stop spinning (vehicle got trapped):", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "53c43d68-a4e9-4a1e-a25a-4090e3bfb4be", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Module[{\n  platform = createPlatform[0.0, 3.0],\n  pen = \
createPendulum[0.00, 9.9, 1.0, 0.003],\n  x = .0,\n  ac = .0,\n  voltage = \
.0,\n  pos = {0., 0.},\n  angle = 0.0,\n  handler\n},\n\n  handler = \
Function[Null,\n    {x, ac} = platform[voltage, 0.01];\n    angle = pen[-ac, \
0.01];\n    pos = {Sin[angle], Cos[angle]};\n  ];\n  \n  \
EventHandler[Graphics[{\n    Translate[{{Brown, Disk[{0,-0.8+1.0}, 0.1]},\n   \
   Rectangle[{-0.4,-1.0+0.2+1.0}, {0.4,-1.0+0.4+1.0}],\n      Red, \
Line[{{0,0.4}, pos// Offload}], Disk[pos// Offload, 0.05]\n    }, {x,-0.1 - \
1.0} // Offload],\n    Line[{{-2.0, -1.0}, {2, -1.0}}],\n    \
EventHandler[AnimationFrameListener[x//Offload], handler]\n  }, \
PlotRange->{{-2,2}, {-1,1}}, ImageSize->{400,200}], {\n    \"mousemove\" -> \
Function[xy, voltage = 2.0 xy[[1]]]\n  }]\n]", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "edf9f67a-bb60-4c61-9045-02cb13447380", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "9c673000-6b4c-436e-b4a6-d378d6d85afc"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nNope, you can't keep it stable with just your \
mouse.\n\n### Add PID\nLet's add a PID controller for the angular position, \
so it will drive our motors to keep the angle of the pendulum at 0. This can \
be illustrated as:", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "9cd0c010-fc03-4b93-8403-f20a01ac15b0", "Invisible" -> False, 
